title: >-
  Modeling Choices in Omics: a browser-based decision lab for the ASHG 2026 workshop
message: If you use or adapt this workshop platform, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Benjamin
    given-names: Kynon J. M.
    affiliation: Northwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2016-4646
  - family-names: Perera
    given-names: Minoli
    affiliation: Department of Pharmacology, Northwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1146-2791
repository-code: https://github.com/heart-gen/modeling-choices-omics-ashg2026
abstract: >-
  A no-code, browser-based educational platform for the ASHG 2026 workshop "Modeling
  Choices in Omics: Implications for Health Disparities in Human Genetics." Participants
  explore six precomputed synthetic genomics scenarios through interactive controls to see
  how analytic decisions - pooled versus stratified analysis, within-ancestry testing
  versus meta-analysis, global versus local ancestry modeling, model complexity,
  regularization, and compute scalability - change biological inference in diverse and
  admixed populations. All statistics are generated offline by a seeded Python generator
  and carry a provenance record distinguishing real reference inputs from synthetic ones.
keywords:
  - human genetics
  - health disparities
  - genetic ancestry
  - admixture
  - statistical genetics
  - research education
  - ELSI
